## Issue-by-Issue Root Cause & Fix

### Issue 1: Onboarding UI not opening for new users

**Root Cause**: In [checkUserAccess()](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/js/shared.js#L413-L497), when a new Google user (non-super-admin) is not found in the `users` collection (line 460), the function returns `false` → the user is signed out and never reaches `loadTenantSettings()` → the `setup_required` event never fires → the onboarding modal never appears.

**Fix**: Auto-provision any new Google user as `TENANT_ADMIN` with a generated `academyId` (based on their email hash), and create their `users` document. This lets them proceed to the dashboard where `loadTenantSettings()` will detect the missing academy doc and fire `setup_required`.

---

### Issue 2: Spot Booking conflict — second user overrides first

**Root Cause**: [checkBookingConflicts()](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/js/shared.js#L511-L543) uses a flat `overlapCount >= 2` threshold for all non-coaching bookings. This doesn't enforce the correct per-type limits.

**Fix**: Rewrite `checkBookingConflicts()` to accept `bookingType` and enforce per-type rules:

```
if bookingType is "Spot booking" or "Advance Training" or "Personal training":
  → Max capacity = 0 existing overlaps (EXCLUSIVE — no other booking allowed)
  
if bookingType is "Members":
  → Max capacity = 6 overlapping members on same court+slot
  → Also reject if an exclusive booking (Spot/Advance/PT) already exists on that slot

if bookingType is "Guest Play":
  → Must have an existing Member booking on same court+slot (guest joins member)
  → Reject if no member booking found

if bookingType is "Coaching":
  → No limit (unlimited students)
  
if bookingType is "Group/Lease":
  → No member count restriction, but reject if exclusive booking exists
```

Also update the **bulk booking path** (line 537-542) to use the same type-aware conflict logic instead of a separate inline check.

---

### Issue 3: Firestore composite index error

**Root Cause**: Queries like `where("date", ">=", ...) + where("date", "<=", ...) + where("academyId", "==", ...)` and `where("court_id", "==", ...) + where("date", "==", ...) + where("academyId", "==", ...")` require composite indexes that don't exist.

**Fix**: Create [firestore.indexes.json](file:///c:/Users/Admin/Documents/POC/Badminton/firestore.indexes.json) with the required indexes. The user must also click the Firestore link in the error message to deploy the indexes in their Firebase console (indexes can't be created from client-side code).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **User Action Required**: After I create the `firestore.indexes.json` file, you need to either:
> 1. Click the link in the Firebase error message to auto-create the index, OR
> 2. Run `firebase deploy --only firestore:indexes` if you have Firebase CLI installed

Additionally, I will **refactor the queries to reduce the number of composite indexes needed** — e.g., by fetching by `academyId` + `date` range and filtering `court_id` client-side.

